### What the patch does

| # | Change | Effect |
|---|--------|--------|
| 1 | Central `try / catch` around the infinite loop | Guarantees *any* exception is caught, preventing the “unhandled rejection” log entry. |
| 2 | Every async call now has explicit error handling (`.catch` or `await …` inside a `try`) | No promise rejection can escape unnoticed. |
| 3 | Exponential back‑off with a cap | Gives the supplier feed time to recover from temporary latency spikes, reducing the likelihood of hitting the retry budget quickly. |
| 4 | `isTransient` helper to differentiate recoverable errors from fatal ones | Allows the loop to keep trying on network glitches while aborting on real bugs. |
| 5 | Global `process.on('unhandledRejection')` logger | Provides a safety net and a clear diagnostic message if a future change forgets to handle a promise. |
| 6 | Reset the back‑off after a successful batch (you can invoke `resetBackoff()` after `processNextBatch` succeeds) | Keeps the delay low for normal operation but grows only when errors persist. |

